helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\sidebar_window.xhp	0	help	par_id2011				0	cs	\<image id=\"img_id2011\" src=\"sfx2/res/symphony/sidebar-template-large.png\" width=\"0.25in\" height=\"0.25in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id2011\"\>Master Pages deck\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\sidebar_window.xhp	0	help	par_id2012				0	cs	The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Master Pages\</item\> deck lists currently used, recently used, and available master pages. Right-click a master page thumbnail for a sub-menu to apply or edit the master page. This deck is only available for presentations.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\sidebar_window.xhp	0	help	par_id2013				0	cs	\<image id=\"img_id2013\" src=\"sfx2/res/symphony/sidebar-animation-large.png\" width=\"0.25in\" height=\"0.25in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id2013\"\>Custom Animation deck\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\sidebar_window.xhp	0	help	par_id2014				0	cs	The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Custom Animation\</item\> deck provides tools to apply animation effects to presentation and graphic objects on your slide. This deck is only available for presentations.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\sidebar_window.xhp	0	help	par_id2015				0	cs	\<image id=\"img_id2015\" src=\"sfx2/res/symphony/sidebar-transition-large.png\" width=\"0.25in\" height=\"0.25in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id2015\"\>Slide Transition deck\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\sidebar_window.xhp	0	help	par_id2016				0	cs	The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Slide Transition\</item\> deck provides tools to apply a special effect that plays when you display a slide. This deck is only available for presentations.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\sidebar_window.xhp	0	help	par_id0002				0	cs	The sidebar is available in WRITER, CALC, IMPRESS, and DRAW application.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\sidebar_window.xhp	0	help	hd_id0500				0	cs	Sidebar Window Handling				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\sidebar_window.xhp	0	help	par_id0003				0	cs	The sidebar is a \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/autohide.xhp\" name=\"docking\"\>dockable window\</link\>. However, you cannot dock it to the bottom or top edge of the working area but only to the left or right edge. The sensitive area for the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command-\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl-\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>double-click method of docking is small, so make sure you click the sidebar window and not its content.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\sidebar_window.xhp	0	help	par_id0004				0	cs	In a docked sidebar window the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Close Sidebar Deck\</item\> button in the upper-right corner of the title area minimizes the current deck, but keeps the tab bar open. To reopen the deck click the corresponding tab or drag the sidebar window frame. To close the sidebar window completely uncheck \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Sidebar\</item\> in the View menu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\sidebar_window.xhp	0	help	par_id0005				0	cs	For decks with several panels click the panel title area to toggle between expanded and minimized state of the panel.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\sidebar_window.xhp	0	help	par_id0006				0	cs	The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>More Options\</item\> button at the top-right of a panel title opens a dialog which provides additional settings. Not all panels have this feature.				20200411 15:09:53
