helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154573	168			0	cs	            \<emph\>Data\</emph\> is the array or range of data in the sample.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3156334	169			0	cs	            \<emph\>Probability\</emph\> is the array or range of the corresponding probabilities.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3151107	170			0	cs	            \<emph\>Start\</emph\> is the start value of the interval whose probabilities are to be summed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3153694	171			0	cs	            \<emph\>End\</emph\> (optional) is the end value of the interval whose probabilities are to be summed. If this parameter is missing, the probability for the \<emph\>Start \</emph\>value is calculated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147574				0	cs	Příklad				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3153666	173			0	cs	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=PROB(A1:A50;B1:B50;50;60)\</item\> returns the probability with which a value within the range of A1:A50 is also within the limits between 50 and 60. Every value within the range of A1:A50 has a probability within the range of B1:B50.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150941				0	cs	\<bookmark_value\>funkce WEIBULL\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
