helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154916				0	cs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_WEIBULL\"\>Vrátí Weibullovo rozdělení.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id0305200911372767				0	cs	The Weibull distribution is a continuous probability distribution, with parameters Alpha > 0 (shape) and Beta > 0 (scale). 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id0305200911372777				0	cs	If C is 0, WEIBULL calculates the probability density function.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id0305200911372743				0	cs	If C is 1, WEIBULL calculates the cumulative distribution function.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159393				0	cs	Syntaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154478				0	cs	WEIBULL(Číslo; Alfa; Beta; C)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3151317	179			0	cs	            \<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value at which to calculate the Weibull distribution.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3158436	180			0	cs	            \<emph\>Alpha \</emph\>is the shape parameter of the Weibull distribution.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154668	181			0	cs	            \<emph\>Beta\</emph\> is the scale parameter of the Weibull distribution.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154825	182			0	cs	            \<emph\>C\</emph\> indicates the type of function.				20200411 15:09:53
